WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.430
- Senator Lindsay Graham
has authored a bill to

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:05.970
ban abortions nationwide
15 weeks after conception,

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.680
with very few exceptions.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.420
- And that is a little more liberal

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.670
than what the Europeans do.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.830
- Now, many have compared
this to European countries

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.020
where generally there is
a minimum of 15 weeks,

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.360
but there's also lots
and lots of exceptions.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.600
- Should we look like Iran and North Korea

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.610
when it comes to national abortion policy?

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.610
Or maybe France, Belgium, Germany, Spain,

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:27.690
Denmark and Norway?

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.730
- And, of course, many European
countries allow abortion

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.280
after 15 weeks, not needing an exception.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.690
Many have criticized this potential law

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.660
as hypocritical, given the
language around states' rights.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.240
This would, of course,
ban abortion nationwide

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.070
and take it out of the state's hands.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.980
- This is where America should
be at the federal level.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.240
- And as we've covered
on this channel before

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.460
given the valence of the
current Supreme Court,

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.724
many people are worried that
a national ban would be held

00:00:49.724 --> 00:00:52.200
up as constitutional by the Supreme Court,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.180
but a national right to abortion

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.250
would not be considered constitutional,

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.013
given the political leanings
of the current justices.

